<title>GERMANY: DG Bank buys software company AMG.</title>
<headline>DG Bank buys software company AMG.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>DG Bank subsidiary DG Diskontbank said on Tuesday it had bought a 60 percent stake in Dortmund-based software company AMG Industrie Consulting GmbH.</p>
<p>The bank said the purchase gave it access to modern communications technology. It did not disclose the purchase price.</p>
<p>Diskontbank said the new subsidiary would enable it to extend its services into the field of sales and purchase financing.</p>
<p>DG Diskontbank said it raised its sales by 16.6 percent to 21 billion marks ($12.7 billion) in 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
<p>($ = 1.653 German Marks)</p>
